WEBVTT

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.250
Stop, Misao!

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.220
Stop!

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:11.830
If you do that...

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:14.650
It's okay.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:16.830
I'm fine.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.090
What are you talking about?

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.820
Your soul is being whittled away!

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.060
There's no way you're fine!

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:31.190
Misao.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.570
Misao!

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.590
Misao!

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.050
This...

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:52.900
...started everything.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.480
I need to see my brother.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:43.010
<i>Asura Cryin' 2</i>

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:30.250
Wow, Shuri!

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.780
What splendid bamboo!

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.830
Tomorrow is Tanabata, after all.

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:35.270
Well?

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:37.210
What am I supposed to do with this?

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:40.380
You write your wish on it and hang it on the tree.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:41.320
Alright.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.170
Let's write some wishes!

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:45.380
Tomo?

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:46.990
Aren't you going to write something?

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:48.580
Oh, no.

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:50.900
Shuri-san...

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.190
...I want to see my brother.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.800
You want to see Naotaka-san? Why?

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:58.800
I want to know what's going on.

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:01.000
I want to know the truth.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.120
Do you know how I can get in touch with my brother?

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:07.230
Unfortunately, no.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:11.730
But didn't you get Kurogane's trunk from him?

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:16.980
That was something the Royal Dark Society had been holding on to.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:20.450
Your brother just asked me to deliver it to you.

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.040
Royal Dark Society?

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:24.150
Who are they?

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:29.440
I think they're an international black science research group...

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.170
...and, uh...

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:34.430
They're Rakurowa High School's Third Student Council's sponsors.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:36.340
Huh?

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.840
Does that mean President Toru...

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:42.220
She might know where Naotaka-san is.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.300
Right! So then...

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.100
You really want to see him?

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:47.100
I see.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.680
In that case, I'll look into it when I have the time.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:52.470
Please do.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:01.370
"The Burial Doll Eaten by the Demon"

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:04.070
Hurry up!

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.510
We'll be late, Tomo!

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:11.860
We barely made it.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.620
Get out of the way!

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:16.000
Vivian!

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:20.200
Mahiwa?

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:35.270
She stopped Vivian with just that sword.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.270
Ow.

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:40.290
You can't come to school on your daughter, Shu Mahiwa.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:43.110
Shuri.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.930
What is President Toru's power?

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:51.920
Kagakagari was surprised to see her, too.

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:55.420
Yeah, because she's an ex-handler.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:56.620
Ex-handler?

00:04:57.390 --> 00:05:00.800
Demons and Asura Machina can't affect her.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.790
She's immune to magic.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.000
Wow!

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:07.850
Doesn't that make her the strongest?

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:10.370
You could be right.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:11.840
Tomo!

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.100
You should become and ex-handler, too!

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.330
Shuri-san, how do you become one?

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:19.540
Oh, well, you know.

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:21.360
More importantly, Tomoharu...

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:24.210
...didn't you need to speak with President Toru?

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:25.060
Right.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:28.530
Oh.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.380
We're late after all.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.140
Look at them!

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:36.460
The Science Club members are like trash!

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.570
You're right! They're trash!

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:42.130
What are they doing?

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:42.950
I don't know.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:45.120
Tokiya! You're here, aren't you?

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:47.740
Tokiya?

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:48.710
Who is that?

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:53.700
Toru, there's no one here with a visual-kei name like that.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.170
He's right there!

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:59.520
Tokiya, they say you didn't go to class today either.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:01.630
What did I tell you yesterday?

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:03.630
Shape up!

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.570
Uh, President Toru...

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:06.920
Tokiya!

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:12.470
The... the koala's dead!

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.200
W-what? No, he's just...

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:17.880
Koala!

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:20.430
Maybe we can still save him!

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:23.160
We just have to jolt him back to life!

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:24.630
Hang in there, koala!

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:28.220
Move.

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:35.620
Touo, draw!

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.670
What is it this time?

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:47.460
This stuffed animal...

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.390
...is a quasi-sensory input/output device made by Tokiya.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:55.860
A quasi-sensory input/output device?

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:59.240
So it's just like a burial doll.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.440
Ow.

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:07.020
With the flip of a switch he can share all five senses with it.

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:08.340
Share?

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.160
With who?

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:14.070
Just so you know, Tokiya is actually a human.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:17.240
He's been hiding in his house and refusing to come to school.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:19.650
What? He's a human?

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.330
What did you think he was?

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:24.940
I thought he might be like Mahiwa's robot Widget.

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:28.460
Well, that's another one of Tokiya's inventions.

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:32.690
Most of my equipment was made by our president as well.

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:36.860
Our president must be pretty amazing.

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:39.100
That tickles!

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:44.210
Koala, does that mean you know a lot about the burial doll system?

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:49.730
He must have cut the connection.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:52.670
I'm leaving.

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:54.640
President Toru!

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:57.490
Do you know where my brother is?

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:58.460
No.

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:00.040
I see.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:03.890
But we could probably contact him...

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:06.940
...through the Royal Dark Society.

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:10.210
They're responsible for Naotaka Natsume.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:11.350
Really?

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:13.880
Do you think you could ask them for me?

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:14.760
Tomo?

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:17.490
Sure. I'll do it.

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:20.130
But there's a condition.

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:21.250
A condition?

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:24.920
As you know, Tokiya refuses to come to school.

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:27.950
In three more days...

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:31.270
...his absences will exceed a third of the total school days.

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:34.820
If that happens, he'll be held back.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:36.170
But more importantly...

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:39.990
...if this continues, he may be expelled.

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:43.690
Tomoharu Natsume.

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:48.280
Make the Science Club president Tokiya Kagayaki return to school.

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:49.330
That is your condition.

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:52.010
If you succeed...

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:56.120
...I'll get Naotaka Natsume's contact information from the Dark Society.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:58.470
Understood. I'll do it.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:08:59.730
Really?

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.580
Uh, yes.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:03.020
Great!

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.310
Good luck, then!

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:06.810
Do whatever it takes to get Tokiya out of his house!

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:13.040
Does she always act like that?

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:14.890
No, I don't think so.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:18.560
She's been acting weird since the koala showed up.

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:20.590
In any case...

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:23.080
...we need to bring the president to school!

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:32.690
President Saeki.

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:34.690
All white? Yuck!

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.600
I see you're with Kanade Takatsuki again.

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:38.480
I'm here, too!

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:39.680
Where are you headed?

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:40.590
Hey, wait!

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:41.470
Is he ignoring me again?

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:44.650
Oh, uh, President Toru asked us...

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:46.140
...to go see the Science Club president.

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:48.140
President Kitsutaka did?

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:49.670
What is that?

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:51.780
It's Hisui's altar.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.690
I'm delivering it to the GD's.

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:56.010
Hisui's altar?

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:57.570
You don't know?

00:09:57.980 --> 00:09:59.570
All Asura Machina...

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:02.120
...have an altar trunk.

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:04.030
Humans that use this altar...

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:08.730
...to offer a burial doll to an Asura Machina...

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.730
...become handlers.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:12.730
There are a few exceptions.

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:13.900
Exceptions?

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:17.280
When a burial doll is sealed...

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:22.220
...but another human is using the Asura Machina.

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:29.380
Two handlers cannot call on the same Asura Machina at once.

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:33.170
Does Kurogane have a previous handler?

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:35.610
Haven't they told you anything?

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:36.140
Huh?

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:37.930
Nevermind.

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:39.690
You'll find out soon enough.

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:41.900
What is this?

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:44.040
This is the president's house?

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:45.540
A bomb shelter?

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:49.710
Well, what are we supposed to do?

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:52.120
We could break it open with Kurogane.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:53.880
What are you talking about?

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:54.910
We can't do that!

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:55.790
Tomo?

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:00.400
Hey guys.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:01.930
How's Tokiya?

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:04.870
What are you two doing here?

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:07.220
What do you mean? I live here.

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:10.040
I'm here to practice with Toru.

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:12.420
What? Then where's the president's house?

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:13.680
Over there.

00:11:15.030 --> 00:11:16.560
You're neighbors!

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:19.060
You don't need me...

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:22.730
...to get him to go to school.

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:25.050
I can't do it.

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:25.870
What?

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:30.070
Misao!

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:31.220
What are you doing?

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:35.800
I was trying to get a look inside.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:41.030
The defense barrier is enchanted.

00:11:41.710 --> 00:11:43.530
Projection bodies can't pass through.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:46.700
I doubt nuclear weapons would do much to it either.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:48.310
Wow.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.310
Can't we just forget it?

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:51.960
He really doesn't want to come out.

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:55.310
It must be because I'm here.

00:11:55.510 --> 00:11:55.830
Huh?

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:57.510
President Toru?

00:11:58.540 --> 00:11:59.360
She left.

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:00.980
Was she angry?

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.410
She's not angry.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:03.530
She's crying.

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:04.180
Huh?

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:06.590
Was she?

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:09.080
She's extremely sad.

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:12.110
So sad she can't even cry tears any more.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:15.310
Did someone die?

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:16.870
Yes.

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:21.360
I'm also familiar with such sadness.

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:26.590
The three of them were childhood friends.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:27.740
Three of them?

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:30.030
You mean President Toru, President Kagayaki, and...

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:33.140
Toru's older sister Aki.

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:38.340
They were great friends.

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:42.220
Aki and Tokiya were especially close.

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:45.330
I couldn't bear to see those two...

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:47.890
...the day Aki died.

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:49.270
You mean...

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:53.000
Aki was Kurogane's burial doll.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:57.730
And the previous owner of Kurogane...

00:12:58.290 --> 00:12:58.790
...was Toru.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:15.710
President!

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:17.140
Can you hear me, president?

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:18.170
Tomo?

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.170
Please come out, president!

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:22.520
Please!

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:23.900
President!

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:28.130
Natsume-kun...

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:37.210
You're brave to have put him through the wash.

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:39.970
He was starting to smell weird.

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:41.000
He needed a good bath.

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:47.430
What's wrong with Tomoharu?

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:49.630
He still hasn't put anything on the tree.

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:50.810
Looks like it.

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:52.660
You think he has too many wishes?

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:53.950
How greedy.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:56.680
It could be the opposite.

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:02.470
Still can't figure out what to wish for?

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:03.380
Yeah.

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:05.580
I'll decide for you!

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:07.020
Let's see.

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.260
"I wish to be smart."

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:10.990
"I wish to be talented."

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:12.340
"I wish to be popular."

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:13.630
What else?

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:19.180
You don't have to worry about me.

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:19.710
Huh?

00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:22.390
I'm fine with things the way they are!

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:25.440
Well, I'm going to bed.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:27.170
See you tomorrow.

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:28.090
Good night!

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:29.760
Good night.

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:36.250
I want to change them.

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:39.510
The fate of handlers...

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:42.010
The fate of burial dolls...

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:45.530
I want to change them.

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:03.720
Naotaka?

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:06.510
You're stupider than I thought...

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:08.480
...Shuri Kurosaki.

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:13.120
Naotaka Natsume is gone.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:14.170
Who are you?

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:16.440
I wonder.

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:20.730
Good bye.

00:15:22.690 --> 00:15:24.130
A phoenix of ice...

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.420
A member of the Torishima family?

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:33.360
Is the club president still hiding?

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:33.940
Yes.

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:35.940
I don't think he's in there.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:38.120
There you are, Tomoharu Natsume!

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:39.060
Yes?

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:41.060
Tokiya is missing!

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:41.580
What?

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:44.460
When I went to his shelter this morning...

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:45.690
...the entrance was open.

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:47.250
Inside I found this.

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:50.390
"I'm going to see Aki."

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:51.830
Going?

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:53.570
To heaven?

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:56.450
Maybe the koala's been inactive because...

00:15:57.590 --> 00:15:58.450
What am I going to do?

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:02.000
Keep it together, Toru.

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:03.350
Susugihara-san.

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:04.380
Tokiya.

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:05.790
Tokiya.

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:08.340
Susugihara-san...

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:11.040
...do you have any idea where he might have gone?

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:12.250
Tokiya?

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:14.360
It can be anywhere.

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:15.920
A store he frequents...

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:17.600
...or somewhere he went with Aki-san.

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:19.420
So there is a place like that.

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:24.120
It could be the place she died.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:29.960
He's here?

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:32.750
Let's find him.

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:34.310
Tokiya!

00:16:35.630 --> 00:16:36.660
Tokiya!

00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:38.250
President!

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:43.970
Tokiya!

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:46.290
No.

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:47.560
This isn't his.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:49.320
President Toru.

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.020
Susugihara-san.

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:54.110
Um...

00:16:54.640 --> 00:16:55.930
What do you want to ask?

00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:59.630
Aki's last moments as a burial doll...

00:17:05.390 --> 00:17:08.910
We were on a mission to subdue an Asura Cryin'.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:14.000
Tokiya was our commander.

00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:14.850
Do it!

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:24.830
Toru!

00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:45.460
It happened suddenly.

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:50.420
Neither Tokiya nor Toru...

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:52.270
...not one of us...

00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:54.770
...had realized Aki's soul was at its limit.

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:04.340
It's nothing special.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:06.580
It's the fate of handlers.

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:11.450
What's important is what you can accomplish in the time you're given.

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:12.690
Tokiya!

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:14.690
Tokiya!

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:16.530
Tokiya!

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:26.700
Tokiya!

00:18:27.810 --> 00:18:28.700
Tokiya!

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:30.870
Wait! Don't go!

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:33.400
Why are you running?

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:34.980
Why?

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:36.600
Because it hurts.

00:18:38.270 --> 00:18:39.650
Seeing my face?

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:43.620
No, you're the one in pain.

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:46.500
When you look at me...

00:18:47.030 --> 00:18:48.790
...you must think of Aki.

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:50.870
Is that why you were hiding?

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:52.200
For my sake?

00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:54.200
Since Aki died...

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:56.200
...I haven't seen you smile.

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:57.540
I...

00:18:58.220 --> 00:19:00.480
I tried to be strong...

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:03.120
...so you wouldn't be in pain any more.

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:04.240
So please...

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:06.800
What? For me?

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:11.440
But I thought you...

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.020
You idiot!

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:15.730
Idiot! You stupid, stupid, stupid moron!

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:17.050
You idiot, Tokiya.

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:19.310
Why would you do that for me?

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:20.630
You really are dumb.

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:23.720
Yeah, but you're stupid, too...

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:26.010
...for worrying about me.

00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:28.330
We're both idiots.

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:33.320
Hey Toru, did you know?

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:35.110
Today is Tanabata.

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:38.200
We can hardly compare ourselves to Orihime and Kengyu...

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:41.370
...but we finally got to see each other again, too.

00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:52.970
Looks like she was finally able to cry.

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:58.850
He's President Kagayaki?

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:01.790
Misao?

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:03.640
Oh, sorry.

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:05.660
I spaced out.

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:16.440
What is all of this?

00:20:16.970 --> 00:20:18.000
Be careful.

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:19.410
President Kagayaki!

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:20.670
Are you in there?

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:22.820
Yeah, I'm just doing some research.

00:20:23.170 --> 00:20:24.460
Uh, president.

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:29.490
It seems the Dark Society couldn't get in touch with Naotaka Natsume either.

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:31.600
I see.

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:36.360
Looks like there's still hope for our world.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:37.530
Huh?

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:39.390
Listen up, Tomoharu Natsume.

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:41.850
Destiny is an excuse.

00:20:42.530 --> 00:20:44.320
Your fate is decided by your choices.

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:45.380
Huh?

00:20:46.610 --> 00:20:47.080
Okay!

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:50.990
Why is that koala here?

00:20:51.490 --> 00:20:53.600
It's easier this way!

00:20:58.300 --> 00:21:00.450
What are you doing about failing or expulsion?

00:21:02.470 --> 00:21:03.530
It'll be fine.

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:06.530
Toru will manipulate the records.

00:21:08.110 --> 00:21:10.050
So you want to grant her wish?

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:13.750
Y-you were eavesdropping?

00:21:14.400 --> 00:21:15.400
If you don't mind...

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:18.340
...I'd love to help you out.

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:23.120
Thank you!

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:29.820
I don't know what you're trying to do...

00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:32.170
...but are you sure want his help? He's a koala.

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:33.410
It'll be fine.

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:35.410
He'll be useless.

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:36.610
I said it's fine.

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:38.430
Tokiya!

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:39.430
Wait, Toru!

00:21:39.930 --> 00:21:41.400
I can explain!

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:42.690
Enough talk!

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:44.420
Touo, draw!

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:47.210
You're dealing with that.

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:49.210
It's fine.

00:23:20.890 --> 00:23:22.770
I don't know small.

00:23:23.060 --> 00:23:23.940
For me?

00:23:24.180 --> 00:23:25.000
I don't know.

00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:27.260
I can't end this fooled.

00:23:27.550 --> 00:23:28.230
Please...

00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:29.140
Please...

00:23:29.490 --> 00:23:30.340
...don't waver.

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:34.980
"Free and Restricted Choices"
